            "value" : "結合 Kᵢ"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Binding strength" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "结合强度"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "結合強度"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Binding used" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "所用结合数据"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "所用結合數據"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Binds to a distinct site on the GABA-A receptor, acting as a positive allosteric modulator that increases the duration of chloride channel opening (unlike benzodiazepines which increase frequency). At higher concentrations, can directly activate GABA-A receptors even without GABA, accounting for their greater overdose lethality. Also inhibits AMPA/kainate glutamate receptors." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "结合于 GABA-A 受体上的一个独特位点,作为正向变构调节剂,增加氯离子通道开放的持续时间(与增加开放频率的苯二氮䓬类不同)。在较高浓度下,即使没有 GABA 也能直接激活 GABA-A 受体,这解释了其更高的过量致死风险。也抑制 AMPA/红藻氨酸盐谷氨酸受体。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "結合於 GABA-A 受體上的一個獨特位點,作為正向變構調節劑,增加氯離子通道開放的持續時間(與增加開放頻率的苯二氮䓬類不同)。在較高濃度下,即使沒有 GABA 也能直接激活 GABA-A 受體,這解釋了其更高的過量致死風險。也抑制 AMPA/紅藻氨酸鹽麩胺酸受體。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Binds to intracellular glucocorticoid receptors, which translocate to the nucleus and modulate gene transcription. Upregulates anti-inflammatory proteins (lipocortins, IL-10) and downregulates pro-inflammatory mediators (cytokines, prostaglandins, leukotrienes). Also suppresses immune cell activation and migration. Metabolic effects include increased gluconeogenesis and altered fat distribution." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "结合于细胞内糖皮质激素受体,这些受体转位至细胞核并调节基因转录。上调抗炎蛋白(脂皮素、IL-10)并下调促炎介质(细胞因子、前列腺素、白三烯)。也抑制免疫细胞的激活和迁移。代谢效应包括糖异生增加和脂肪分布改变。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "結合於細胞內糖皮質激素受體,這些受體轉位至細胞核並調節基因轉錄。上調抗炎蛋白(脂皮素、IL-10)並下調促炎介質(細胞因子、前列腺素、白三烯)。也抑制免疫細胞的激活和遷移。代謝效應包括糖異生增加和脂肪分布改變。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Binds to penicillin-binding proteins (PBPs) on the bacterial cell membrane, inhibiting transpeptidation — the final step in bacterial cell wall (peptidoglycan) synthesis. This weakens the cell wall, leading to osmotic lysis and bacterial death. Bactericidal against susceptible organisms. Inactivated by bacterial β-lactamase enzymes (overcome by combining with clavulanate)." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "结合于细菌细胞膜上的青霉素结合蛋白 (PBP),抑制转肽作用 — 即细菌细胞壁(肽聚糖)合成的最后一步。这削弱细胞壁,导致渗透性裂解和细菌死亡。对敏感菌有杀菌作用。被细菌的 β-内酰胺酶灭活(可通过与克拉维酸合用克服)。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "結合於細菌細胞膜上的青黴素結合蛋白 (PBP),抑制轉肽作用 — 即細菌細胞壁(肽聚醣)合成的最後一步。這削弱細胞壁,導致滲透性裂解和細菌死亡。對敏感菌有殺菌作用。被細菌的 β-內醯胺酶滅活(可透過與克拉維酸合用克服)。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Binds to the 50S ribosomal subunit of bacterial ribosomes, inhibiting translocation of peptidyl-tRNA and blocking protein synthesis. Bacteriostatic at typical concentrations. Has a very long tissue half-life and accumulates in phagocytes, which transport it to sites of infection. Also has anti-inflammatory and immunomodulatory properties." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "结合于细菌核糖体的 50S 亚基,抑制肽基-tRNA 的转位,阻断蛋白质合成。在典型浓度下为抑菌剂。组织半衰期非常长,并在吞噬细胞中蓄积,后者将其运送到感染部位。也具有抗炎和免疫调节特性。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "結合於細菌核糖體的 50S 亞基,抑制肽基-tRNA 的轉位,阻斷蛋白質合成。在典型濃度下為抑菌劑。組織半衰期非常長,並在吞噬細胞中蓄積,後者將其運送到感染部位。也具有抗炎和免疫調節特性。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Binds to the benzodiazepine site at the interface of α and γ subunits on GABA-A receptors, acting as a positive allosteric modulator. Enhances the effect of GABA by increasing the frequency of chloride channel opening, leading to neuronal hyperpolarization and reduced excitability. Produces anxiolytic, sedative, hypnotic, anticonvulsant, and muscle relaxant effects." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "结合于 GABA-A 受体上 α 和 γ 亚单位界面的苯二氮䓬位点,作为正向变构调节剂。通过增加氯离子通道开放频率增强 GABA 的效应,导致神经元超极化和兴奋性降低。产生抗焦虑、镇静、催眠、抗惊厥和肌肉松弛效应。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "結合於 GABA-A 受體上 α 和 γ 亞單位界面的苯二氮䓬位點,作為正向變構調節劑。透過增加氯離子通道開放頻率增強 GABA 的效應,導致神經元超極化和興奮性降低。產生抗焦慮、鎮靜、催眠、抗驚厥和肌肉鬆弛效應。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Binds to the benzodiazepine site on GABA-A receptors with preferential selectivity for the α1 subunit, which is predominantly associated with sedation and hypnosis. This selectivity produces hypnotic effects with less anxiolytic, anticonvulsant, and muscle relaxant activity compared to benzodiazepines, though selectivity diminishes at higher doses." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "结合于 GABA-A 受体的苯二氮䓬位点,对 α1 亚单位具有优先选择性,后者主要与镇静和催眠相关。这种选择性产生催眠效应,而抗焦虑、抗惊厥和肌肉松弛活性比苯二氮䓬类少,但在较高剂量下选择性会减弱。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "結合於 GABA-A 受體的苯二氮䓬位點,對 α1 亞單位具有優先選擇性,後者主要與鎮靜和催眠相關。這種選擇性產生催眠效應,而抗焦慮、抗驚厥和肌肉鬆弛活性比苯二氮䓬類少,但在較高劑量下選擇性會減弱。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Binds to the α2δ-1 subunit of voltage-gated calcium channels (VGCCs), reducing calcium influx at presynaptic nerve terminals. This decreases the release of excitatory neurotransmitters including glutamate, norepinephrine, substance P, and calcitonin gene-related peptide. Despite the name, gabapentinoids do not interact with GABA receptors or GABA metabolism." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "结合于电压门控钙通道 (VGCC) 的 α2δ-1 亚单位,减少突触前神经末梢的钙内流。这减少兴奋性神经递质(包括谷氨酸、去甲肾上腺素、P 物质和降钙素基因相关肽)的释放。尽管名字如此,加巴喷丁类药物并不与 GABA 受体或 GABA 代谢相互作用。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "結合於電壓門控鈣通道 (VGCC) 的 α2δ-1 亞單位,減少突觸前神經末梢的鈣內流。這減少興奮性神經傳導物質(包括麩胺酸、去甲腎上腺素、P 物質和降鈣素基因相關肽)的釋放。儘管名字如此,加巴噴丁類藥物並不與 GABA 受體或 GABA 代謝相互作用。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "bioavailability" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "生物利用度"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "生物利用度"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Bioavailability" : {

    },
    "Bioavailability (F)" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "生物利用度 (F)"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "生物利用度 (F)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Bioavailability versus dose: gabapentin falls as the dose rises, pregabalin stays flat." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "生物利用度随剂量的变化：加巴喷丁随剂量升高而下降，普瑞巴林保持平稳。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "生物利用度隨劑量的變化：加巴噴丁隨劑量升高而下降，普瑞巴林保持平穩。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Biweekly" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "两周一次"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "兩週一次"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Bliss" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "极乐"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "極樂"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks 5-HT₂A while weakly inhibiting serotonin reuptake. The receptor block dominates at low doses, which is why trazodone reached far more people as a sleep drug than as an antidepressant." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻断5-HT₂A，同时弱抑制5-羟色胺再摄取。低剂量时受体阻断占主导，这就是曲唑酮作为助眠药比作为抗抑郁药触及了多得多的人的原因。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻斷5-HT₂A，同時弱抑制血清素回收。低劑量時受體阻斷佔主導，這就是曲唑酮作為助眠藥比作為抗憂鬱藥觸及了多得多的人的原因。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks dopamine D2 receptors in the mesolimbic pathway, reducing dopaminergic neurotransmission associated with positive psychotic symptoms. Also blocks D2 receptors in the nigrostriatal pathway (causing extrapyramidal symptoms), tuberoinfundibular pathway (causing hyperprolactinemia), and mesocortical pathway. Most also antagonize histamine H1, muscarinic, and α1-adrenergic receptors to varying degrees." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻断中脑边缘通路中的多巴胺 D2 受体,减少与阳性精神病症状相关的多巴胺能神经传递。也阻断黑质纹状体通路(引起锥体外系症状)、漏斗结节通路(引起高催乳素血症)和中脑皮质通路中的 D2 受体。大多数还不同程度地拮抗组胺 H1、毒蕈碱和 α1-肾上腺素受体。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻斷中腦邊緣通路中的多巴胺 D2 受體,減少與陽性精神病症狀相關的多巴胺能神經傳導。也阻斷黑質紋狀體通路(引起錐體外系症狀)、漏斗結節通路(引起高泌乳素血症)和中腦皮質通路中的 D2 受體。大多數還不同程度地拮抗組胺 H1、蕈毒鹼和 α1-腎上腺素受體。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks L-type voltage-gated calcium channels in vascular smooth muscle, reducing calcium influx and causing vasodilation. Primarily acts on arterial smooth muscle with minimal cardiac effects at therapeutic doses. Reduces peripheral vascular resistance and blood pressure." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻断血管平滑肌中的 L 型电压门控钙通道,减少钙内流并引起血管扩张。主要作用于动脉平滑肌,治疗剂量下心脏影响极小。降低外周血管阻力和血压。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻斷血管平滑肌中的 L 型電壓門控鈣通道,減少鈣內流並引起血管擴張。主要作用於動脈平滑肌,治療劑量下心臟影響極小。降低外周血管阻力和血壓。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks N-methyl-D-aspartate (NMDA) glutamate receptors, typically by binding within the ion channel pore as a non-competitive antagonist. NMDA receptor blockade reduces excitatory glutamatergic neurotransmission, producing dissociative anesthesia, analgesia, and altered states of consciousness characterized by feelings of detachment from body and environment." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻断 N-甲基-D-天冬氨酸 (NMDA) 谷氨酸受体,通常作为非竞争性拮抗剂结合于离子通道孔内。NMDA 受体阻断减少兴奋性谷氨酸能神经传递,产生解离性麻醉、镇痛和以与身体和环境脱离感为特征的意识改变状态。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻斷 N-甲基-D-天門冬胺酸 (NMDA) 麩胺酸受體,通常作為非競爭性拮抗劑結合於離子通道孔內。NMDA 受體阻斷減少興奮性麩胺酸能神經傳導,產生解離性麻醉、鎮痛和以與身體和環境脫離感為特徵的意識改變狀態。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks NMDA glutamate receptors as a non-competitive antagonist. Also inhibits the dopamine transporter (DAT), increasing synaptic dopamine — this dopaminergic activity distinguishes PCP from other dissociatives and contributes to its stimulant properties and higher psychosis risk. Additionally interacts with sigma receptors, nicotinic receptors, and voltage-gated sodium channels." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作为非竞争性拮抗剂阻断 NMDA 谷氨酸受体。也抑制多巴胺转运体 (DAT),增加突触多巴胺 — 这种多巴胺能活性使 PCP 区别于其他解离剂,并对其兴奋特性和更高的精神病风险有贡献。另外与 sigma 受体、烟碱受体和电压门控钠通道相互作用。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作為非競爭性拮抗劑阻斷 NMDA 麩胺酸受體。也抑制多巴胺轉運體 (DAT),增加突觸多巴胺 — 這種多巴胺能活性使 PCP 區別於其他解離劑,並對其興奮特性和更高的精神病風險有貢獻。另外與 sigma 受體、菸鹼受體和電壓門控鈉通道相互作用。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks noradrenaline and dopamine reuptake, leaving serotonin alone — the activating end of the family." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻断去甲肾上腺素和多巴胺的再摄取，不动5-羟色胺——这一类里偏兴奋的一端。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻斷正腎上腺素和多巴胺的回收，不動血清素——這一類裡偏興奮的一端。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks presynaptic α2-adrenergic autoreceptors and heteroreceptors, increasing norepinephrine and serotonin release. Simultaneously blocks 5-HT2A, 5-HT2C, and 5-HT3 receptors, directing serotonergic activity through 5-HT1A receptors. Potent histamine H1 antagonism produces marked sedation and appetite stimulation, particularly at lower doses where antihistaminic effects predominate." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻断突触前 α2-肾上腺素自身受体和异源受体,增加去甲肾上腺素和血清素释放。同时阻断 5-HT2A、5-HT2C 和 5-HT3 受体,将血清素能活性导向 5-HT1A 受体。强效组胺 H1 拮抗产生明显的镇静和食欲刺激,特别是在低剂量下抗组胺效应占主导。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻斷突觸前 α2-腎上腺素自身受體和異源受體,增加去甲腎上腺素和血清素釋放。同時阻斷 5-HT2A、5-HT2C 和 5-HT3 受體,將血清素能活性導向 5-HT1A 受體。強效組胺 H1 拮抗產生明顯的鎮靜和食慾刺激,特別是在低劑量下抗組胺效應佔主導。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks reuptake without triggering release (cocaine/methylphenidate-type) — a different tolerance and redose profile from a releaser." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻断再摄取但不促进释放（可卡因／哌甲酯类）——其耐受性与再用药特征与释放剂不同。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻斷再攝取但不促進釋放（古柯鹼／派醋甲酯類）——其耐受性與再用藥特徵與釋放劑不同。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks serotonin and noradrenaline reuptake like an SNRI, and also histamine, muscarinic and α₁ receptors. That extra binding is the sedation, the dry mouth, and the narrow margin in overdose." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "像SNRI一样阻断5-羟色胺和去甲肾上腺素的再摄取，同时还结合组胺、毒蕈碱和α₁受体。多出来的这部分结合，就是镇静、口干，以及过量时安全窗口狭窄的来源。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "像SNRI一樣阻斷血清素和正腎上腺素的回收，同時還結合組織胺、蕈毒鹼和α₁受體。多出來的這部分結合，就是鎮靜、口乾，以及過量時安全窗口狹窄的來源。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks serotonin and noradrenaline reuptake together. The noradrenaline share grows with dose, so a low dose can behave much like an SSRI." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "同时阻断5-羟色胺和去甲肾上腺素的再摄取。去甲肾上腺素那一份随剂量增大，因此低剂量时表现可以很像SSRI。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "同時阻斷血清素和正腎上腺素的回收。正腎上腺素那一份隨劑量增大，因此低劑量時表現可以很像SSRI。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks the dopamine (DAT), norepinephrine (NET), and serotonin (SERT) transporters, preventing reuptake and increasing synaptic monoamine levels. Unlike amphetamines, cocaine inhibits reuptake without reversing transporter function or releasing stored neurotransmitters. The rapid onset and short duration of DAT blockade contribute to its high addiction potential. Also blocks voltage-gated sodium channels, producing local anesthetic effects." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻断多巴胺 (DAT)、去甲肾上腺素 (NET) 和血清素 (SERT) 转运体,阻止再摄取并提高突触单胺水平。与苯丙胺类不同,可卡因抑制再摄取而不反转转运体功能或释放储存的神经递质。DAT 阻断的快速起效和短持续时间助长其高成瘾潜力。也阻断电压门控钠通道,产生局部麻醉效应。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻斷多巴胺 (DAT)、去甲腎上腺素 (NET) 和血清素 (SERT) 轉運體,阻止再攝取並提高突觸單胺水平。與苯丙胺類不同,古柯鹼抑制再攝取而不反轉轉運體功能或釋放儲存的神經傳導物質。DAT 阻斷的快速起效和短持續時間助長其高成癮潛力。也阻斷電壓門控鈉通道,產生局部麻醉效應。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks the dopamine transporter (DAT) and norepinephrine transporter (NET), increasing synaptic dopamine and norepinephrine. Unlike amphetamines, methylphenidate is a pure reuptake inhibitor — it does not reverse transporter function or release stored monoamines. Preferentially increases catecholamines in the prefrontal cortex and striatum, enhancing attention, working memory, and executive function." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻断多巴胺转运体 (DAT) 和去甲肾上腺素转运体 (NET),增加突触多巴胺和去甲肾上腺素。与苯丙胺类不同,哌甲酯是纯再摄取抑制剂 — 不反转转运体功能或释放储存的单胺。优先增加前额叶皮质和纹状体中的儿茶酚胺,增强注意力、工作记忆和执行功能。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻斷多巴胺轉運體 (DAT) 和去甲腎上腺素轉運體 (NET),增加突觸多巴胺和去甲腎上腺素。與苯丙胺類不同,哌甲酯是純再攝取抑制劑 — 不反轉轉運體功能或釋放儲存的單胺。優先增加前額葉皮質和紋狀體中的兒茶酚胺,增強注意力、工作記憶和執行功能。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks the enzyme that breaks monoamines down, rather than the transporters that recycle them, so all three rise. The tyramine restriction and the long interaction list both follow from that." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻断的是分解单胺的酶，而不是回收它们的转运体，所以三种单胺都会升高。酪胺饮食限制和那一长串相互作用，都由此而来。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻斷的是分解單胺的酶，而不是回收它們的轉運體，所以三種單胺都會升高。酪胺飲食限制和那一長串交互作用，都由此而來。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks the serotonin transporter and little else, which is why its effects and its side effects are both mostly serotonergic." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "几乎只阻断5-羟色胺转运体，因此它的作用与副作用大多都是5-羟色胺性的。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "幾乎只阻斷血清素轉運體，因此它的作用與副作用大多都是血清素性的。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blocks β1, β2, and α1-adrenergic receptors, providing combined vasodilation and cardiac output reduction. The α1 blockade produces direct arterial vasodilation, distinguishing it from pure β-blockers. Also has antioxidant and anti-proliferative properties that may provide additional cardiovascular protection beyond blood pressure lowering." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻断 β1、β2 和 α1-肾上腺素受体,提供血管扩张和心输出量降低的联合效应。α1 阻断产生直接的动脉血管扩张,与纯 β-阻滞剂有所不同。也具有抗氧化和抗增殖特性,可能在降低血压之外提供额外的心血管保护。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "阻斷 β1、β2 和 α1-腎上腺素受體,提供血管擴張和心輸出量降低的聯合效應。α1 阻斷產生直接的動脈血管擴張,與純 β-阻滯劑有所不同。也具有抗氧化和抗增殖特性,可能在降低血壓之外提供額外的心血管保護。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blood pressure" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "血压"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "血壓"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Blood pressure, heart, and cholesterol." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "血压、心脏与胆固醇。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "血壓、心臟與膽固醇。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "body" : {
      "comment" : "What the 5-HT1A pole of the balance arc governs",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "身体"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "身體"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Body content" : {

    },
    "Body load" : {

    },
    "Body Weight" : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "体重"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "體重"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Boiling point" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "沸点"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "沸點"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Both bind the α2δ-1 calcium-channel subunit — but gabapentin rides a saturable intestinal carrier (system-L / LAT1), so the fraction absorbed drops as the dose climbs (~60% → ~27%) and exposure flattens out. That's why gabapentin is dosed several times a day and why very large single doses buy little extra. Pregabalin uses the carrier without saturating it, so it stays ~90% absorbed at any dose — predictable, dose-proportional, simpler to titrate. (Pregabalin is also effective at far fewer milligrams, so its line sits at the low end of the dose axis.)" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "两者都结合电压门控钙通道的 α2δ-1 亚基——但加巴喷丁依赖一种可饱和的肠道载体（system-L／LAT1），因此随着剂量升高，吸收的比例下降（约 60% → 约 27%），暴露量趋于平缓。这正是加巴喷丁每日需分多次服用、以及单次大剂量收效甚微的原因。普瑞巴林利用同一载体但不会使其饱和，因此在任何剂量下都保持约 90% 的吸收——可预测、与剂量成比例、更易于滴定。（普瑞巴林在低得多的毫克数下即有效，因此其曲线位于剂量轴的低端。）"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "兩者都結合電壓門控鈣通道的 α2δ-1 亞基——但加巴噴丁依賴一種可飽和的腸道載體（system-L／LAT1），因此隨著劑量升高，吸收的比例下降（約 60% → 約 27%），暴露量趨於平緩。這正是加巴噴丁每日需分多次服用、以及單次大劑量收效甚微的原因。普瑞巴林利用同一載體但不會使其飽和，因此在任何劑量下都保持約 90% 的吸收——可預測、與劑量成比例、更易於滴定。（普瑞巴林在低得多的毫克數下即有效，因此其曲線位於劑量軸的低端。）"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Both can lower blood pressure and add to dizziness — you may feel faint, especially standing up." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "两者都会降低血压并增加头晕——可能感到眩晕，尤其是起身时。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "兩者都會降低血壓並增加頭暈——可能感到眩暈，尤其是起身時。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Both cause drowsiness — expect additive next-day sedation and grogginess. Use less and don't drive." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "两者都会引起困倦——次日镇静和昏沉会相加。请减量，且不要开车。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "兩者都會引起睏倦——隔日鎮靜和昏沉會相加。請減量，且不要開車。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
