    "Methadone's potency rises with dose (nonlinear) and its long, variable half-life makes any single factor unsafe. CDC removed its conversion factor. Never back-calculate a methadone dose from MME — this must be done by a clinician." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "美沙酮的效价随剂量升高（非线性），且半衰期长而多变，任何单一换算系数都不安全。CDC 已取消其换算系数。切勿根据 MME 反推美沙酮剂量——这必须由临床医生完成。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "美沙酮的效價隨劑量升高（非線性），且半衰期長而多變，任何單一換算係數都不安全。CDC 已取消其換算係數。切勿根據 MME 反推美沙酮劑量——這必須由臨床醫生完成。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Methylphenidate and alcohol together form ethylphenidate — an active stimulant your body makes only while both are present. It leans more on dopamine and lingers a little longer than methylphenidate, so the stimulant effect is drawn out." : {

